-by-dates-and-consuming-foods-past-the-use-by-dates","verified":"Food Standards Agency guidance recommends a fridge temperature of 5 degrees Celsius or below.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"FOOD_HYGIENE_03","direct_score_input":false},{"row":94,"status":"PASS_FOOD_HYGIENE_04","source":"Food Standards Agency food hygiene","url":"https://www.food.gov.uk/research/behaviour-and-perception/not-checking-use-by-dates-and-consuming-foods-past-the-use-by-dates","verified":"Food businesses in England, Wales and Northern Ireland must keep cold food below 8 degrees Celsius.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"FOOD_HYGIENE_04","direct_score_input":false},{"row":95,"status":"PASS_FOOD_HYGIENE_05","source":"Food Standards Agency food hygiene","url":"https://www.food.gov.uk/research/behaviour-and-perception/not-checking-use-by-dates-and-consuming-foods-past-the-use-by-dates","verified":"Cooked food should be cooled quickly and placed in the fridge within 1 to 2 hours.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"FOOD_HYGIENE_05","direct_score_input":false},{"row":96,"status":"PASS_FOOD_HYGIENE_06","source":"Food Standards Agency food hygiene","url":"https://www.food.gov.uk/research/behaviour-and-perception/not-checking-use-by-dates-and-consuming-foods-past-the-use-by-dates","verified":"Chilled foods should be kept out of refrigeration for the shortest practical time during preparation.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"FOOD_HYGIENE_06","direct_score_input":false},{"row":97,"status":"PASS_FOOD_HYGIENE_07","source":"Food Standards Agency food hygiene","url":"https://www.food.gov.uk/research/behaviour-and-perception/not-checking-use-by-dates-and-consuming-foods-past-the-use-by-dates","verified":"Food should not be supplied or served after its use-by date.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"FOOD_HYGIENE_07","direct_score_input":false},{"row":98,"status":"PASS_FOOD_HYGIENE_08","source":"Food Standards Agency food hygiene","url":"https://www.food.gov.uk/research/behaviour-and-perception/not-checking-use-by-dates-and-consuming-foods-past-the-use-by-dates","verified":"Food businesses should use a food-safety management system and maintain suitable temperature-check routines and records.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"FOOD_HYGIENE_08","direct_score_input":false},{"row":99,"status":"PASS_WITH_FOOD_HYGIENE_09","source":"Food Standards Agency food hygiene","url":"https://www.food.gov.uk/food-hygiene","verified":"Food-hygiene controls depend on product, process, temperature history, equipment, staff practice, shelf life and consumer vulnerability.","quality_score":"3","adoption":"FOOD_HYGIENE_GUARD_09","direct_score_input":false},{"row":100,"status":"PASS_WITH_FOOD_HYGIENE_10","source":"Food Standards Agency food hygiene","url":"https://www.food.gov.uk/food-hygiene","verified":"Food-hygiene evidence is product-, process- and time-specific and is not an exact parcel-level foodborne-illness probability.","quality_score":"3","adoption":"FOOD_HYGIENE_GUARD_10","direct_score_input":false}]}